  3	/**
  4	 * What the cohorts are actually doing, said cheaply.
  5	 *
  6	 * DEV TOOLING — read-only, never shipped behaviour, never run in a universe. Run it in the GRAND or
  7	 * PVE app container, never the dev stack: those two are the real cohorts.
  8	 *
  9	 *   docker compose -f local-docker-dev/docker-compose.grand.yml exec -T ogamex-app \
 10	 *     sh -lc "cd /var/www && php artisan tinker --execute=\"require '/var/www/Modules/AI/scripts/verify-cohorts.php';\""
 11	 *
 12	 * The default pass is SQL counters plus one aggregate per defence object — about twenty queries, so
 13	 * it answers instantly on a 20-account cohort. The per-account detail is expensive on purpose (it
 14	 * builds the real perception, which runs every planner) and is therefore opt-in: pass ids, e.g.
 15	 *   ... --execute="\$argv = [12]; require '.../verify-cohorts.php';"
 16	 */
